{"item_id": "youtube:euc3l6kCUZI", "version_id": "71a4911f50701803a0027e37535c1d30aef2c4b4a45ef5cbeb543e2137b32852", "decision": "reject", "reason": "The transcript consists only of the word \"Heat\" and music, with no substantive content about gear, so it fails the Accept criteria and falls under the rejection rule for promotional posts with no substantive content (Making the decision). Gatorz is an eyewear manufacturer with a Vortex x Gatorz collaboration, so the commercial tie to a title sponsor is noted under Commercial incentives, but it does not change the outcome here.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "youtube:Uv4CSksQBPE", "version_id": "dfcd82afaed693f0863259f75d4f20c8e56e70d763fdd9d8909189a6d8c5a20a", "decision": "reject", "reason": "The transcript contains only the word \"you,\" with no substantive gear content, so it does not meet the Making the decision standard for acceptance and is rejected as a post with no substantive content. The publisher's rangefinder and ballistic-calculator testing history is noted, and its possible Element Seeker brand relationship is unverified under Commercial incentives, but neither changes the outcome.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "youtube:knDbFj2S4Yo", "version_id": "825537d2b2e97b3ef74693b900d7a6d0da0a53506351b49399b8da2f97b86584", "decision": "reject", "reason": "The transcript contains only the closing line \"We'll see you next time,\" so there is no evidence about MDT DRT or poi shift testing for the Relevance rules to apply to. Under Making the decision, this is a post with no substantive content and is rejected; the unchecked possible Element Seeker relationship under Commercial incentives does not alter the result.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "youtube:0ohADGu1uCI", "version_id": "b59e837e4556ba550db58849339b48abd99f59fec12d5de06cf2c88d53facede", "decision": "reject", "reason": "The transcript contains only the word \"Alright\" and the title refers to a heli-gunning video, which falls under the Relevance rule rejecting hunting tactics and game content, and in any case there is no substantive gear evidence. Under Making the decision, it is rejected as out of scope and as a post with no substantive content.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "youtube:ocKDJ7xuzkE", "version_id": "d54a81fa1bcd2dc622a4427937808e16cc78fcc22fa40741a975dcc9921a16a7", "decision": "defer", "reason": "The transcript shows a rangefinder reading (655,656 yards, 4.8 miles of elevation correction, 0.3 left) and a wind call, which are in-scope spotting and measuring content under Relevance, but the reading is a single unverified demonstration with no independent test, measured comparison, or sponsorship check, so it lacks the evidence specificity needed under Credibility and Making the decision. The publisher's frequent Element Seeker coverage may indicate a brand relationship that is unverified under Commercial incentives; defer until more evidence is available.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "youtube:io9b9ALY1aU", "version_id": "2bf1ba02f879aefa84ba018c1388a3655e600453c1822b3eef400b1635ff306e", "decision": "reject", "reason": "The transcript contains only the word \"pop,\" with no substantive gear content, and the title centers on a firearm and rifle, which falls under the Exclusions rule against reviews of firearms and chassis. Under Making the decision, it is rejected as a post with no substantive content.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "podcast:c219e3c1-b26c-4c37-882b-759af3f892df", "version_id": "706d57c181a240186c295b4643878e60ca99444061848ae779b70d1546c83cba", "decision": "accept", "reason": "The episode substantively covers down insulation, fill power, down-to-feather ratio, treated versus untreated DWR down, baffle design, and sleeping bag temperature ratings, all in scope under the Relevance categories for cold-weather layers and sleep systems, and it addresses Mammoth-relevant conditions such as wetness, packed weight, and durability. Under Credibility, the claims mostly rest on Argali's own testing and on a self-described \"unscientific\" water submersion test, which is noted as weak evidence, and the host's claims are unsupported by independent data; under Commercial incentives, Argali is a manufacturer and the episode is a sponsored brand segment hosted by Vortex, a Mammoth sponsor, so its praise and marketing claims (such as \"ISO testing\" and \"treated down is overblown\") should be treated as manufacturer claims. Piece 02 is the best fit because it asks what manufacturer claims hold up under testing, and the DWR-versus-untreated and comfort-versus-limit rating disputes are exactly the kinds of claims to present with attribution.", "piece_ids": ["02"]}
